  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">220681_FY23_UNICEF_Kenya_(&amp; Extension #3) Nutrition Drought Emergency Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome: Strengthened capacities and improved access to life saving health and nutrition services for children under five and pregnant women to mitigate the effects of prolonged drought in Turkana, Marsabit, Samburu and Baringo Counties. 
 
 Project will target 141,451 (69,311boys and 72,140 girls) under 5 years, 75,209 pregnant and lactating women across the four targeted Counties.</narrative>
  </description>
